WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.130
The funny guy from a Japanese movie, Itami Juzo, succeeded in making that sweet home into a Famicom.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.170
Five TV reporters are trapped in a cursed mansion.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.320
It's your duty to control these five people and get as many people out as you can.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.440
Ah, run away! If you keep whining, you'll be killed in the mansion!

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.800
Be careful in the dark! A evil creature is waiting for you!

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.730
I don't know anything about everyone! I'm going to run away by myself!

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.910
That kind of guy will be killed right away!

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.360
If you all work together and help each other, you can't escape!

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.160
Even if I get killed, you will escape!

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.230
Will you be able to escape from the cursed mansion?

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:45.860
Depending on the number of people who escape, 5 moving endings await you!

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.130
An adventure of love and fear!

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.460
Sweet Home The Famicom

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.440
Give me the power of your heart!

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:00.990
Yeah.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:36.450
But now, the situation is unstable.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:43.000
Yop!

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:51.280
Akiko-san, you're late.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.440
I'm sure you're in a hurry.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.530
Hey, Akiko-san.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.430
Shouldn't you go cheer them on?

00:02:59.260 --> 00:02:59.880
Don't worry.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.090
Don't worry. It'll take some time.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.530
No matter how many times you lower your head, you can't do anything impossible.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.830
Well, I can't help it.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.600
I've told you many times.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.770
I refuse to enter your mansion.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.360
It's on TV, so I'll admit it's an exception.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:19.610
It's a bit too much of a bug.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:25.480
Listen, there's a picture of Ichiro Mamiya in that mansion.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.160
It's the last painting of Ichiro Mamiya.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.640
It's our duty to introduce such a valuable cultural asset to the world.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.300
Otaku is also a persistent person.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.300
Speaking of TV, I thought that a countryman would shake his head.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.420
Hey, what's wrong?

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:50.540
They say they want to see Mamiya-tei over there.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.930
Mamiya-tei? No, no, no, it won't be a problem.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.480
It's been closed there for 30 years.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.300
What is the purpose?

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.970
In fact, the TV station...

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:05.180
There's the last mural of Ichiro Mamiya in that mansion.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.150
The TV station?

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:07.730
Yes.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.950
They're making a TV show about Ichiro Mamiya.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.200
It's a kind of travel show.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:19.140
Are you from the TV station?

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:23.960
It's about introducing your hometown,

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:25.390
cooking together,

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:26.740
going to hot springs.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.990
It's that kind of show, isn't it?

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:33.210
That's fine, but since you're here,

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.580
why don't you talk about the 1000-year anniversary of Kamiko Touge?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.370
Miki's father is the best in Japan.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.190
Why don't you talk about that?

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.010
Well...

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.720
Dad's really weak-willed.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.290
He's always with his wife.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.880
He can't say what he wants to say.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.970
And he's a producer.

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:56.550
Don't say that about your father, Michi.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:58.320
That's right.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:04:59.860
Mom's dead.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.360
It's as if he's become more and more like a father since he was a child.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.200
I'm almost a babysitter, you know?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.040
Babysitter?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.620
Hey, this is my babysitter, isn't it?

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.100
Taguchi-san is Asuka-san, right?

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:10.700
No way.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.040
Asuka-san, you're so cold.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:52.990
Is that all right, sir? What if something happens?

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:55.780
What do you mean?

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.600
The rumors about the Mamia family.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:03.420
Tatarika?

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:03.720
Yes.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.260
Then why don't you check it out when you go there?

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.230
What do you mean?

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:22.250
Without a gun, that mansion would be a source of great tourism.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:27.940
Even if something happens every day, this is a supernatural phenomenon.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.230
I can't take responsibility for it.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:35.390
Then this is the key to the Mamiya house.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:45.260
you

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:11.630
You can't do that.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.750
I'm going to do it myself.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.190
I've finally got my license.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.420
Thank you for watching.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.800
Hi Asuka-chan, how are you?

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.340
Let's go inside.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:10.130
Is it not opening?

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:16.840
You're still going in?

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:21.860
No, wait.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:23.230
No.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:53.180
I don't think so.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.290
Try harder.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.040
It's off.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:44.890
I've just entered Mamiya-tei.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.240
There's a lot of dust all over the place.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:50.070
It smells like mold.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.600
I'm very worried if the mural is safe.

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:56.860
That's a bad sound.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:12.020
30 years ago, genius painter Ichiro Mamiya took a deep breath here.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:16.750
Since then, the Mamiya family has been in disarray without a trace.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:21.840
For decades, no one has been able to step in as a victim.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.010
What's that sound?

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.470
Everyone, be careful. There's a lot of people in this house.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.740
They're all here.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:50.300
They're not here yet.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:52.520
They're here.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.000
It's out of power, too.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:01.500
Oh, really?

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:06.090
Yes, it's my house.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:10.410
If it's a mansion like this, there should be a generator somewhere, right?

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:12.740
Power...

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:43.730
Let's get to work.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:47.480
First, let's get some dust and look at the painting.

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:52.200
I'm the one who repairs the painting, so I'll do everything.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:39.240
Emi, your coffee's in. Do you want some?

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:44.800
Dad, Kiko-san is working.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:47.120
Why don't you bring her some coffee?

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:51.880
Why do you have to do that?

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:54.800
If you keep whining, someone will take it away from you.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:57.940
I'll put up with it if it's her.

00:15:57.980 --> 00:15:59.310
It's about time for me to settle down.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.840
You're not young anymore, Dad.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:11.150
What are you talking about?

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:14.510
I'm not always at home.

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:17.420
You should have decided on this trip.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:20.420
I came here with that in mind.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:23.720
You've become so much like your mother.

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:24.140
What?

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:26.370
You're just like your dead mother.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.600
I know, right?

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:33.130
That's right. I'm going to explore the house.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.420
Do you want coffee?

00:17:50.572 --> 00:17:51.212
Here we go.

00:17:54.476 --> 00:17:55.856
I'm walking with her.

00:17:56.396 --> 00:17:57.656
I think I'll be back soon.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:03.900
He's a celebrity. He grew up playing alone.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.940
He's always been a kid.

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:06.680
I see.

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:10.130
You want him to stay as a kid forever?

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.310
That's not true.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:12.950
I want him to be a married man.

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:17.840
Then he'll be independent again.

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:20.080
There's a lot of things he wants to do.

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:22.860
And he's still alive.

00:19:32.652 --> 00:19:34.612
What's wrong? Where have you been?

00:19:35.212 --> 00:19:37.092
You have to do what you have to do first.

00:19:37.868 --> 00:19:38.868
What an idiot!

00:19:39.436 --> 00:19:41.096
It's a summer break now.

00:19:41.516 --> 00:19:45.656
Besides, it's not your father who told you to study hard at the shooting site.

00:19:45.996 --> 00:19:47.996
Thank you for watching until the end.

00:19:52.844 --> 00:19:54.844
Why don't you all come with me?

00:19:54.924 --> 00:19:55.924
Something's strange.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.440
There's a painting here, too.

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:04.300
And here, too.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.790
It's a painting.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:20.480
Is it a door?

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:23.320
Isn't this a flame?

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:28.490
Is it a flame? It's dark.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:30.840
It's a tree.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:31.760
It's a human.

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:34.770
That's the hair.

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:36.050
This is the face.

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:39.360
Which is it?

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:41.320
Is it a black hole-like eye?

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:42.100
What?

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:45.160
It's the jaw.

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:47.110
It's a grave.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:52.600
It's a face.

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:54.770
Isn't the head small?

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:56.950
It's the face of a baby.

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:05.460
It's half broken!

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:22.420
Let's watch the other two scenes.

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:26.530
The picture that was shown in the video

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.910
This is a sub-picture.

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:29.550
What is this?

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:30.440
It was written without a plan.

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:35.900
So the composition is not finalized.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:42.360
It's impossible for a single fresco artist to change the plan during the process.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:49.270
It's certainly strange. What does it mean?

00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:53.260
This is something that happened on the way home that I didn't expect.

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:58.710
Or he was in some kind of mental shock.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:01.510
I guess I had to change my husband a lot.

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:09.660
It's a story suitable for the legendary painter Ichiro Mamiya.

00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:13.810
But I wonder what the case is.

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:20.250
Let's split up and look for more houses.

00:22:20.350 --> 00:22:21.500
Maybe we'll find a way to solve some secrets.

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:23.100
Please stop.

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:23.860
Why?

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:25.620
I'm the one reporting.

00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:28.180
I'm going to make this program my own.

00:22:28.820 --> 00:22:29.500
Case.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.100
I'm going to find out the secret of the documentary.

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:32.480
You guys just have to shoot it.

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:33.680
This is my show.

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:34.960
Wait a minute, Asuka.

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:37.900
A documentary is...

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:40.730
You have to run with everyone, right?

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:43.650
You report.

00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:46.070
Taguchi turns the camera.

00:22:47.370 --> 00:22:48.350
I'll judge the situation.

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:52.110
This is everyone's show.

00:22:53.710 --> 00:22:54.690
It can't be your own show.

00:22:55.790 --> 00:22:57.800
Aki, wait a minute.

00:22:57.960 --> 00:22:59.680
What are you waiting for?

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:03.820
Let's make it clear that this is related to the principle of work

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:05.140
I understand

00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:07.040
I'm sorry to say something unnecessary

00:23:07.480 --> 00:23:09.230
Please continue to talk

00:23:09.230 --> 00:23:12.430
Let's explore

00:23:12.430 --> 00:23:27.300
I was in the storage

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:29.240
Isn't it cool?

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:42.440
What are you doing?

00:23:47.560 --> 00:23:56.420
Asuka-chan is right.

00:23:56.780 --> 00:23:58.610
Don't get in the way of my house.

00:24:25.150 --> 00:24:26.850
This is a beautiful color.

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:28.740
Do you want to go to bed?

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:31.140
This is my mom's.

00:24:31.300 --> 00:24:34.540
When I was little, she always wore this.

00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:39.940
Oh, when you wear it, it reminds you of your mom, doesn't it?

00:24:40.780 --> 00:24:44.160
No, Mom, it's getting farther and farther away.

00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:45.620
Even if I try to remember it with my eyes closed,

00:24:47.220 --> 00:24:50.880
I can only see something like light, so I can't tie it up.

00:24:51.320 --> 00:24:55.600
Oh, what's your dad saying?

00:24:57.310 --> 00:24:59.420
This is the cruelest part of life.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.810
He thinks it's a good place and a nice place, too.

00:25:04.950 --> 00:25:07.010
Then your father will feel sorry for you.

00:25:07.270 --> 00:25:14.060
Kiko-san, aren't you getting married?

00:25:14.580 --> 00:25:18.600
I'm going to get married someday.

00:25:19.660 --> 00:25:21.020
Why don't you get married?

00:25:21.650 --> 00:25:22.910
Hurry up and get married.

00:25:23.190 --> 00:25:27.300
Even if you say that, it's not good for you.

00:25:31.850 --> 00:25:32.450
Akiko-san,

00:25:32.510 --> 00:25:35.220
What about children?

00:25:35.460 --> 00:25:36.650
Don't you give birth to a newborn?

00:25:37.510 --> 00:25:46.780
Akiko-san,

00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:53.420
How about giving this to them?

00:25:53.560 --> 00:25:54.820
I'm sure it'll fit them.

00:25:55.020 --> 00:25:58.380
Don't do that.

00:26:02.360 --> 00:26:04.360
It's best for Emi to wear it with care.

00:26:04.560 --> 00:26:09.410
She'll be happy.

00:26:09.770 --> 00:26:12.940
It's too small.

00:26:13.300 --> 00:26:18.010
Don't take it off.

00:26:18.190 --> 00:26:19.010
No, I can't.

00:26:19.150 --> 00:26:20.890
Wear something like a skirt or a jacket.

00:26:22.170 --> 00:26:24.360
No, it's too small.

00:26:24.820 --> 00:26:27.860
You're pretty independent.

00:26:28.480 --> 00:26:29.490
You're the mother.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:34.080
You have to be more independent, like me.

00:26:34.080 --> 00:26:34.860
Akiko won't come.

00:26:37.350 --> 00:26:38.870
Look, shoes, shoes.

00:26:39.210 --> 00:26:39.870
Oh, no.

00:26:40.070 --> 00:26:41.740
I know, I know.

00:26:42.020 --> 00:26:43.080
You're a noisy woman.

00:26:43.600 --> 00:26:45.460
I want to see the face of a man who marries a woman like you.

00:26:48.260 --> 00:26:50.950
I'm going to turn it off.

00:26:51.110 --> 00:26:51.940
Wait a minute.

00:26:52.390 --> 00:26:55.060
It's going to be dark.

00:26:57.450 --> 00:26:58.390
Wait a minute.

00:26:58.390 --> 00:26:59.660
It's going to be dark.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.900
Let's go to the bathroom.

00:27:02.900 --> 00:27:03.360
Okay.

00:27:04.160 --> 00:27:05.350
Good night.

00:27:06.860 --> 00:27:08.280
Good night.

00:28:07.070 --> 00:28:21.480
My baby. Give me back my baby.

00:29:00.800 --> 00:29:01.000
Thank you.

00:31:02.620 --> 00:31:04.680
15 seconds, 28-21.

00:31:05.120 --> 00:31:07.580
Will he manage to get back on track?

00:31:07.700 --> 00:31:09.240
We don't know yet.

00:31:09.820 --> 00:31:20.920
He's running!

00:31:21.160 --> 00:31:22.150
He's changing the course!

00:31:27.150 --> 00:31:28.590
75 yards!

00:31:35.310 --> 00:31:36.670
Now, Nascar's first down.

00:31:36.750 --> 00:31:37.750
The quarterback is out.

00:31:37.930 --> 00:31:38.830
It's a pass.

00:31:39.110 --> 00:31:40.050
It's a pass.

00:31:40.450 --> 00:31:42.820
It's a pass.

00:31:43.110 --> 00:31:44.630
Go, go, go, go!

00:32:05.500 --> 00:32:09.110
It's the lever over there.

00:32:09.150 --> 00:32:09.960
It's the red one.

00:32:10.100 --> 00:32:16.390
It's the other one.

00:32:16.870 --> 00:32:17.520
It's the upper one.

00:32:31.340 --> 00:32:31.840
Ugh!

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:04.930
But it's not the white one. It's the real one.

00:33:05.210 --> 00:33:09.390
I don't need it.

00:33:13.120 --> 00:33:15.370
Mr. Yamamura, that's a problem.

00:33:16.200 --> 00:33:19.290
You remembered my name. I'm glad.

00:33:19.630 --> 00:33:22.110
But I can't get money from the benefactor of life.

00:33:32.490 --> 00:33:33.460
Thank you.

00:33:33.460 --> 00:33:35.350
Thank you very much.

00:33:36.750 --> 00:33:38.110
What are you doing with so much gas?

00:33:39.170 --> 00:33:40.000
I'm using it for electricity.

00:33:40.640 --> 00:33:42.950
I'm filming a TV show.

00:33:43.330 --> 00:33:44.710
A TV show?

00:33:44.950 --> 00:33:46.830
Hey, wait a minute!

00:34:01.470 --> 00:34:02.630
Let's start, please.

00:34:02.970 --> 00:34:13.530
Taguchi, let's make her move.

00:34:15.130 --> 00:34:16.430
Yes, ma'am.

00:34:16.610 --> 00:34:16.990
Wait.

00:34:18.360 --> 00:34:21.310
Let's put the camera on the wheelchair.

00:34:21.810 --> 00:34:22.330
Okay.

00:34:22.980 --> 00:34:24.110
Emi.

00:34:24.290 --> 00:34:24.750
Yes.

00:34:25.330 --> 00:34:25.860
Bring the wheelchair.

00:34:26.340 --> 00:34:26.580
It's outside.

00:34:27.180 --> 00:34:27.660
Okay.

00:34:40.910 --> 00:34:42.360
Huh? What's this?

00:34:42.700 --> 00:34:51.050
You're here, Emi?

00:34:51.370 --> 00:34:51.770
Yeah.

00:34:53.670 --> 00:34:53.950
Move.

00:35:04.590 --> 00:35:23.700
What are you doing?

00:35:30.250 --> 00:35:31.490
I don't remember anything at all.

00:35:31.750 --> 00:35:33.830
It must be the mold.

00:35:34.370 --> 00:35:36.980
Sorry to bother you.

00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:41.000
I'm going home.

00:36:14.940 --> 00:36:15.480
I'll go to the hospital.

00:36:15.640 --> 00:36:17.850
Please, Emi.

00:36:17.850 --> 00:36:20.500
But please come back soon.

00:36:20.740 --> 00:36:22.270
I may have to get up.

00:36:23.110 --> 00:36:24.090
So please pack your things.

00:36:24.510 --> 00:36:25.350
And your father's too.

00:36:26.210 --> 00:36:26.610
Yes.

00:36:27.210 --> 00:36:28.620
How is it?

00:36:28.720 --> 00:36:29.340
Can you fix it?

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:32.520
It's an electric wire.

00:36:32.900 --> 00:36:36.120
It's a pain in the ass.

00:36:36.880 --> 00:36:38.960
I'll go get a tester.

00:36:39.500 --> 00:36:44.290
It fell off.

00:36:47.940 --> 00:36:49.820
How's Asuka?

00:36:50.060 --> 00:36:51.410
She's not badly injured,

00:36:51.410 --> 00:36:52.850
but she shouldn't hit her head,

00:36:53.170 --> 00:36:54.370
so we should take her to the hospital.

00:36:54.790 --> 00:36:56.350
But the car...

00:36:56.350 --> 00:36:58.210
I'll go to the gas station and call them.

00:36:58.610 --> 00:36:59.940
I'll be there in 30 minutes.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.660
Don't worry, I'll go.

00:37:02.900 --> 00:37:04.300
No, please stay here.

00:37:04.600 --> 00:37:05.700
I have to go.

00:37:06.120 --> 00:37:06.680
What?

00:37:06.920 --> 00:37:15.660
Don't you think it's strange?

00:37:16.380 --> 00:37:16.940
What?

00:37:18.290 --> 00:37:19.870
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:37:21.790 --> 00:37:24.020
But this house is strange.

00:37:24.260 --> 00:37:27.520
There's a baby buried there.

00:37:27.880 --> 00:37:29.810
That's a grave, isn't it?

00:37:30.250 --> 00:37:31.130
It's common in the countryside.

00:37:31.450 --> 00:37:33.750
That's because Asuka, who dug it out, became like that.

00:37:34.050 --> 00:37:34.530
Asuka?

00:37:36.210 --> 00:37:38.300
She was originally a strange woman.

00:37:38.700 --> 00:37:41.510
Please, don't mess with me and listen to me.

00:37:43.280 --> 00:37:47.730
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:37:47.930 --> 00:37:58.760
If I stay here, something bad will happen.

00:38:00.350 --> 00:38:00.910
That's what I feel.

00:38:01.350 --> 00:38:01.750
Really?

00:38:02.980 --> 00:38:07.220
Do you believe in things like Tataris?

00:38:07.520 --> 00:38:09.540
I'm worried about them.

00:38:11.580 --> 00:38:13.400
Besides, Mr. Kazuo is 100 years old this year.

00:38:14.520 --> 00:38:17.000
What's so funny?

00:38:17.360 --> 00:38:18.660
It's funny, isn't it?

00:38:18.840 --> 00:38:20.420
It's actually interesting.

00:38:20.940 --> 00:38:21.700
What's so funny?

00:38:22.120 --> 00:38:25.750
What's so funny? Do you believe in things like that?

00:38:25.870 --> 00:38:29.980
Occult, blood type, star fortune-telling, Nostradamus...

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.970
It's a new discovery, it's Aki-chan's new charm

00:38:36.710 --> 00:38:39.100
It's not strange

00:38:39.620 --> 00:38:41.890
Why can't you listen seriously when people are talking seriously?

00:38:43.270 --> 00:38:45.470
I think that's very insensitive

00:38:45.470 --> 00:38:47.680
No, I'm going to praise it

00:38:48.020 --> 00:38:49.360
I can't praise it

00:38:49.360 --> 00:38:51.100
I don't know how people feel

00:38:51.100 --> 00:38:53.770
It's not like that, I ...

00:38:53.770 --> 00:38:54.810
You don't know

00:38:54.810 --> 00:38:59.460
Even my feelings, Emi-chan's feelings, Mr. Kazuo doesn't understand anything

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:00.120
What?

00:39:00.440 --> 00:39:01.930
How's Aki-chan?

00:39:02.550 --> 00:39:11.700
I'm sorry. I just got up.

00:40:09.276 --> 00:40:11.276
Tsuka-san?

00:40:19.548 --> 00:40:21.548
Asuka-san...

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:59.980
Thank you.

00:42:00.090 --> 00:42:02.220
What's wrong? Emi, what's wrong?

00:42:02.480 --> 00:42:03.320
I can't breathe!

00:42:03.500 --> 00:42:04.560
I can't breathe!

00:42:05.290 --> 00:42:05.950
Emi!

00:42:46.830 --> 00:42:49.460
Oh, that scared me!

00:42:49.980 --> 00:42:57.900
What happened here?

00:43:04.760 --> 00:43:05.240
Asuka...

00:43:09.340 --> 00:43:11.450
What's wrong?

00:43:15.090 --> 00:43:15.530
You're feeling down?

00:43:15.830 --> 00:43:18.000
Yeah...

00:43:18.090 --> 00:43:19.420
Don't be so upset.

00:43:33.160 --> 00:43:33.700
Do you want me to dunk you?

00:43:34.340 --> 00:43:42.380
You're a piece of shit.

00:45:00.640 --> 00:45:00.860
uh

00:45:30.508 --> 00:45:31.108
No!

00:46:14.428 --> 00:46:14.928
It's the-

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:04.990
It's not dead.

00:49:13.530 --> 00:49:15.200
What's wrong with him?

00:49:15.200 --> 00:49:17.520
He'll watch us.

00:49:17.820 --> 00:49:19.520
Wait. Don't leave him.

00:49:20.260 --> 00:49:21.790
This place is scary.

00:49:22.350 --> 00:49:26.570
Let's go together.

00:49:51.628 --> 00:49:53.628
What are you talking about?

00:50:00.670 --> 00:50:03.870
What do you think this is? It's the Kuyo tower.

00:50:04.170 --> 00:50:06.160
The Kuyo tower?

00:50:06.300 --> 00:50:07.880
You're the one who broke it.

00:50:08.220 --> 00:50:09.160
No, it wasn't me.

00:50:09.460 --> 00:50:11.060
It just collapsed naturally.

00:50:11.300 --> 00:50:13.960
Mr. Yamamura, we don't know anything.

00:50:14.320 --> 00:50:17.180
Aki, do you know her?

00:50:17.460 --> 00:50:19.400
Yes, Mr. Yamamura from the gas station.

00:50:21.360 --> 00:50:22.680
She's the owner, right?

00:50:23.460 --> 00:50:23.840
No.

00:50:24.270 --> 00:50:25.970
If you're done talking, go home.

00:50:26.490 --> 00:50:29.500
You don't have the right to say that!

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:35.590
I have the right.

00:50:35.950 --> 00:50:39.630
What happened here?

00:50:39.870 --> 00:50:41.760
It has nothing to do with us.

00:50:41.820 --> 00:50:42.940
Anyway, go home.

00:50:43.100 --> 00:50:44.260
I don't want to go home.

00:50:44.400 --> 00:50:44.840
I can't go home.

00:50:45.080 --> 00:50:48.840
I have two children left.

00:50:50.900 --> 00:50:52.060
Anyway, let's find Asuka and Taguchi.

00:50:55.830 --> 00:50:58.400
Hey, don't go inside the house.

00:51:08.280 --> 00:51:08.860
Hey, Takuchi!

00:51:09.040 --> 00:51:10.610
Takuchi-kun!

00:51:10.810 --> 00:51:19.740
Asuka! Takuchi!

00:51:20.020 --> 00:51:28.920
Kazuo-san, I think we should have Mr. Yamamura come with us.

00:51:30.640 --> 00:51:32.040
Let's get rid of that rambunctious guy.

00:51:33.080 --> 00:51:34.860
Dad, let's get out of here.

00:51:35.120 --> 00:51:36.220
Don't be stupid.

00:51:36.840 --> 00:51:40.150
Chi! Chi!

00:54:21.400 --> 00:54:22.720
What happened?

00:54:23.080 --> 00:54:24.330
What happened?

00:54:24.650 --> 00:54:26.470
Mr. Yamamura!

00:54:26.770 --> 00:54:28.130
Mr. Yamamura!

00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:03.520
See you later, mom.

00:55:49.580 --> 00:55:58.480
3, 2, 1, go!

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:00.220
I'm here.

00:56:00.360 --> 00:56:04.590
We can live together.

00:56:04.770 --> 00:56:15.720
What are you doing?

00:56:15.960 --> 00:56:17.540
Hurry up.

00:56:17.980 --> 00:56:26.750
Emi, who are you?

00:56:35.050 --> 00:56:35.770
She's not your daughter!

00:56:36.330 --> 00:56:38.030
What do you mean?

00:57:01.390 --> 00:57:28.040
What the hell are you doing?

00:58:08.400 --> 00:58:10.920
What's wrong?

00:58:12.890 --> 00:58:13.690
What happened?

00:58:14.150 --> 00:58:24.440
30 years ago, a baby was born in the family of Kamiya.

00:58:24.440 --> 00:58:27.550
Ichiro was happy.

00:58:27.870 --> 00:58:29.900
My child's growth...

00:58:30.190 --> 00:58:37.390
I tried to draw the story on one side of the wall, but the happiness didn't last long.

00:58:37.690 --> 00:58:46.370
In the morning, Mrs. Mamiya went down to the basement as usual and twisted the cock of the incinerator.

00:58:46.610 --> 00:58:51.160
Why did she do that?

00:58:51.240 --> 00:58:59.020
A baby who had just started to walk entered the incinerator.

00:59:00.500 --> 00:59:05.840
It was already too late when the baby was taken out.

00:59:06.760 --> 00:59:10.650
My mother also had severe burns and lost one of her eyes.

00:59:11.170 --> 00:59:18.080
After the incident, many children from this area were killed.

00:59:18.900 --> 00:59:22.350
It was Mrs. Mamia.

00:59:22.990 --> 00:59:28.820
She took care of the children in the village and threw them into the incinerator.

00:59:30.960 --> 00:59:32.240
Why did you do such a terrible thing?

00:59:32.500 --> 00:59:34.100
It's a child's playmate.

00:59:34.620 --> 00:59:39.300
It's lonely to be alone, isn't it?

00:59:39.940 --> 00:59:42.830
That's why I brought a playmate.

00:59:47.460 --> 00:59:49.980
The villagers came to Mamiya-tei to find out the truth.

00:59:50.080 --> 00:59:56.870
Mrs. Mamiya closed herself up to the incinerator.

01:00:01.980 --> 01:00:06.440
Mrs. Mamiya is dead. Ichiro is also dead.

01:00:06.580 --> 01:00:10.590
But Ichiro continued to draw until he died.

01:00:10.910 --> 01:00:15.110
That's the story of the Mamiya family.

01:00:16.210 --> 01:00:23.390
I have to find Emi.

01:00:23.490 --> 01:00:27.200
Emi, what happened to Emi?

01:00:28.220 --> 01:00:29.220
What's going on in this house now?

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:34.610
It's all because of you two who saved Mrs. Mamiya in the dark.

01:00:36.860 --> 01:00:37.700
What's going on?

01:00:38.270 --> 01:00:43.170
The darkness in the dark? The shadow in the shadow?

01:00:43.250 --> 01:00:43.590
It's all because of you two!

01:00:44.650 --> 01:00:48.220
Asha, let's go find Emi.

01:00:49.360 --> 01:00:50.940
But what should we do?

01:00:51.300 --> 01:00:53.590
Let's go to the sewers and gather the light.

01:00:55.300 --> 01:00:59.600
You don't know anything about this, do you?

01:01:00.480 --> 01:01:01.740
Yamamura-san, what should we do?

01:01:02.120 --> 01:01:05.030
Emi was taken in by the darkness.

01:01:05.190 --> 01:01:08.100
Light it up and erase the darkness.

01:01:08.300 --> 01:01:09.640
Emi will never find it.

01:01:09.760 --> 01:01:10.660
I've done it all.

01:01:11.280 --> 01:01:15.350
How can you still not understand that you're just making the other person angry?

01:01:16.750 --> 01:01:18.120
That's what you're saying.

01:01:18.440 --> 01:01:19.900
Even your protection didn't do any good.

01:01:20.760 --> 01:01:22.310
As long as you can light it up.

01:01:22.310 --> 01:01:23.690
If you can light it up, you can make a shadow.

01:01:24.390 --> 01:01:28.540
Even if you can light it up, what about the darkness inside you?

01:01:29.020 --> 01:01:29.980
Inside me...

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:31.360
You can't do anything about it with your fist in your hand.

01:01:31.920 --> 01:01:40.930
What's important is concentration, the power of your heart.

01:01:41.270 --> 01:01:48.590
If you make it stronger, your bones will really break.

01:01:48.790 --> 01:01:52.010
It won't be useful if you're a coward.

01:02:02.200 --> 01:02:02.560
No

01:02:05.080 --> 01:02:15.220
Do you have a child?

01:02:15.720 --> 01:02:16.260
No

01:02:18.740 --> 01:02:19.220
Alone?

01:02:20.730 --> 01:02:21.030
Yes

01:02:24.250 --> 01:02:27.760
Then it's difficult

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:34.470
It's not easy for a woman to win over her mother.

01:02:36.330 --> 01:02:40.000
A mother who has lost her child...

01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:43.000
...and a mother who has lost her child...

01:02:43.000 --> 01:02:44.120
...are fighting each other.

01:02:46.060 --> 01:02:48.160
You can't take Emi back like this.

01:02:49.590 --> 01:02:50.550
You don't want me to be a father?

01:02:51.510 --> 01:02:55.730
Try crushing her.

01:03:02.780 --> 01:03:03.660
It's not the time to say that!

01:03:03.780 --> 01:03:05.100
Emi may be dead!

01:03:05.880 --> 01:03:06.740
I know where your daughter is!

01:03:07.720 --> 01:03:09.180
Calm down.

01:03:09.300 --> 01:03:13.490
It's a way to calm her down,

01:03:13.490 --> 01:03:17.090
but it's surprisingly useful to increase her concentration with this.

01:03:17.830 --> 01:03:22.650
If you can crush it, you're a genius.

01:03:37.520 --> 01:03:41.220
It's a waste of time. We can't go on like this.

01:03:41.360 --> 01:03:42.760
Emi is in danger.

01:03:43.000 --> 01:03:43.400
But...

01:04:00.990 --> 01:04:28.250
Te tai wa boshi ni ratoku sume azawai sema

01:04:30.600 --> 01:04:44.020
Even if you try to tell me, I can't help but think that you're old enough to protect me.

01:04:55.120 --> 01:04:55.680
No!

01:05:01.690 --> 01:05:02.090
Oh

01:06:14.350 --> 01:06:28.350
What's wrong with the lights?

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:30.720
If you do, you'll be in big trouble.

01:07:03.130 --> 01:07:03.330
Thank you.

01:07:31.020 --> 01:07:31.860
It's in the incinerator.

01:07:32.320 --> 01:07:33.210
It's captured by the ghost of Lady Amiya.

01:07:34.630 --> 01:07:38.480
Don't worry. I'll save you.

01:08:42.110 --> 01:08:56.640
Hit him properly!

01:08:56.760 --> 01:08:57.340
I'm hitting him!

01:08:57.680 --> 01:08:59.590
Don't you want to go?

01:09:01.180 --> 01:09:16.320
You must have had a happy past.

01:09:17.020 --> 01:09:20.260
You must have had many happy memories.

01:09:21.580 --> 01:09:24.240
Please, give me back my daughter.

01:09:26.000 --> 01:09:26.820
Emi is still a child.

01:09:27.200 --> 01:09:29.060
Emi still needs parents.

01:09:30.920 --> 01:09:31.640
You know that, don't you?

01:09:31.640 --> 01:09:34.140
You're already dead!

01:09:35.160 --> 01:09:37.180
Why don't you know that?

01:09:37.820 --> 01:09:45.220
I'm fine, I'm fine.

01:09:45.380 --> 01:09:48.380
Leave the girl alone and get out of here!

01:09:48.840 --> 01:09:59.440
Wait for me, I'm coming!

01:10:02.990 --> 01:10:04.230
POTATES

01:11:18.040 --> 01:11:25.460
I'm going to kill you!

01:14:00.700 --> 01:14:01.240
I'll be back soon.

01:14:01.300 --> 01:14:02.810
Don't go to a dark place.

01:14:03.170 --> 01:14:03.950
Stay in the cell.

01:14:04.370 --> 01:14:05.030
Got it?

01:14:05.680 --> 01:14:11.140
Idiot!

01:14:30.830 --> 01:14:31.290
Da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da.

01:15:33.070 --> 01:15:34.140
Aki-chan, are you okay?

01:15:36.070 --> 01:15:36.690
Damn it!

01:15:36.690 --> 01:15:40.680
Aki-chan, I'm going to go.

01:15:40.960 --> 01:15:41.240
Good.

01:15:43.200 --> 01:15:44.700
Emi has come out.

01:15:44.920 --> 01:15:46.930
You take Emi and run away.

01:15:49.590 --> 01:15:50.890
I'll run away even if I can't.

01:15:50.970 --> 01:15:54.900
If you can get back safely.

01:18:08.480 --> 01:18:08.900
Please give me strength.

01:21:30.540 --> 01:21:33.650
Don't hide in the crime scene forever and come out here!

01:22:34.188 --> 01:22:34.448
Thank you.

01:24:01.180 --> 01:24:04.310
Please, don't make us suffer!

01:26:01.850 --> 01:26:02.070
Thank you.

01:27:03.770 --> 01:27:04.350
I'm trying to hide it.

01:28:01.212 --> 01:28:01.712
No!

01:33:09.756 --> 01:33:11.756
Thank you for watching!

01:37:36.040 --> 01:37:36.200
You

01:38:15.100 --> 01:38:15.460
I'm sorry.

01:38:35.468 --> 01:38:36.228
I'll talk to you later.
